From 7ea84a1b1e175b1e6fb78124593b4feb0e78dcb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:39:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer useful CopyDrafts continuations and prune aligned
 suffix search

Rank longest-level matches by available continuation length (1..lookahead)
before recency, stop backward suffix search once any lane in the warp
finds a full-continuation match at the current longest level, advance each
warp's required match length across lanes as shorter levels are matched and
probe the anchor tokens at need_len and need_len // 2 before walking a
candidate suffix, gate copy replacement in copy_apply against DSpark's
expected yield (offered * estimate >= sum(dspark_confidences[r, :block]))
while clearing pending copy state when DSpark wins, keep the two-stage
32-element aligned forward-coalesced tile scan in copy_match_kernel with
priority decoding in copy_alloc_kernel, and grow the adaptive draft cap
from 1 -> 8 -> 16 on clean full-hit acceptance.
Upstream base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a
Rationale: Rank longest-level CopyDrafts matches by continuation length before recency, stop backward suffix search once any lane hits a full-continuation longest match, prune shorter-level scans with warp-min need_len and 2-token anchor probes, and gate copy replacement against DSpark expected yield.
Quality: Restores 8->16 adaptive copy drafts on repetitive tails, cuts 1M-token suffix scans by 28-90x, and prevents low-yield copy proposals from clobbering higher-expected-yield DSpark drafts.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py and benchmark_copy_drafts.py --gate across 2 fresh container boots.
Upstream status: Local CopyDrafter suffix-search and expected-yield optimization.
